IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tas-nouns`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1931 (Tasmania), ss 1 to 4: title, repeal, "regulation", the limits of legislative power, and the application of the Act.
-- Answers of a rule of reading: JUST TRUE where the text applies to the case; JUST FALSE only where the text itself says no to the case in its own words
--   (a "means" definition, a condition introduced with "if", "only if", "as long as" or "unless", a list closed with "only", a flat negative, a "where" that fails, a period the text fixes and the case falls outside it);
-- NOTHING everywhere else (an open list, "includes", a term left undefined, silence, a pointer outside the sources, a grant or prohibition limited by its own wording where the case falls outside the limit, a scope limit with no "only").
-- A rule that returns a day, a name or a value has no second not-covered answer, so it returns NOTHING when its text does not apply.
-- Not encoded as rules (machinery, see NOTES.md): s 1 (short title) and s 2 (repeal of three earlier Acts); s 4(4) is shown only as a row of dots.

§ `s 2A: "regulation"`

-- src:25 | 2A. Meaning of "regulation"
-- src:27 | In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears,
-- src:29 | regulation includes rule and by-law.
@ref s 2A (src:25-29)
GIVEN `the instrument` IS A `Kind of instrument`
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2A: an instrument is within the word regulation in this Act` `the instrument` `the contrary intention appears` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the instrument` EQUALS `a regulation` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `the instrument` EQUALS `a rule` THEN IF `the contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE
           IF `the instrument` EQUALS `a by-law` THEN IF `the contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 2A: an instrument is within the word regulation in this Act` `a rule` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2A: an instrument is within the word regulation in this Act` `a by-law` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2A: an instrument is within the word regulation in this Act` `a regulation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2A: an instrument is within the word regulation in this Act` `a rule` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2A: an instrument is within the word regulation in this Act` `a by-law` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2A: an instrument is within the word regulation in this Act` `a proclamation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 3: subject to the legislative powers of the State`

-- src:31 | 3. Acts to be construed subject to legislative powers of State
-- src:33 | Every Act shall be read and construed subject to the limits of the legislative powers of the State and so as not to exceed such powers, to the intent that, where any enactment thereof, but for this provision, would be construed as being in excess of such powers, it shall nevertheless be a valid enactment to the extent to which it is not in excess of such powers.
@ref s 3 (src:31-33)
GIVEN `the part is within the legislative powers of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3: a part of an enactment takes effect as an enactment` `the part is within the legislative powers of the State` MEANS
    `the part is within the legislative powers of the State`

#ASSERT `s 3: a part of an enactment takes effect as an enactment` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3: a part of an enactment takes effect as an enactment` FALSE)

§ `s 4(1): the Act applies to every Act and regulation, except in so far as`

-- src:37 | (1) Except where otherwise expressly provided, the provisions of this Act shall be applied in the interpretation and construction of every Act whenever passed (including this Act) and of all regulations made under any Act, except in so far as –
-- src:39 | (a) any provision of this Act is inconsistent with or repugnant to the true intent and object of the particular Act or regulation to be interpreted; or, in case of a regulation, with the true intent and object of the Act under which such regulation purports to have been made;
-- src:41 | (b) the interpretation which any provision of this Act would give to anything contained in such particular Act or regulation is inconsistent with the context thereof or with any definition or interpretation contained in such particular Act or regulation or in the Act under which such regulation is made.
@ref s 4(1) (src:37-41)
GIVEN `the instrument` IS A `Kind of instrument`
      `otherwise expressly provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision of this Act is inconsistent with or repugnant to the true intent and object of the instrument or of its authorising Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interpretation a provision of this Act would give is inconsistent with the context or with a definition or interpretation in the instrument or its authorising Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1): the provisions of this Act apply in interpreting the instrument` `the instrument` `otherwise expressly provided` `a provision of this Act is inconsistent with or repugnant to the true intent and object of the instrument or of its authorising Act` `the interpretation a provision of this Act would give is inconsistent with the context or with a definition or interpretation in the instrument or its authorising Act` MEANS
    IF `the instrument` EQUALS `an Act` OR `the instrument` EQUALS `a regulation` OR `the instrument` EQUALS `a rule` OR `the instrument` EQUALS `a by-law`
    THEN JUST (NOT (`otherwise expressly provided` OR `a provision of this Act is inconsistent with or repugnant to the true intent and object of the instrument or of its authorising Act` OR `the interpretation a provision of this Act would give is inconsistent with the context or with a definition or interpretation in the instrument or its authorising Act`))
    ELSE NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 4(1): the provisions of this Act apply in interpreting the instrument` `an Act` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1): the provisions of this Act apply in interpreting the instrument` `a regulation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1): the provisions of this Act apply in interpreting the instrument` `an Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1): the provisions of this Act apply in interpreting the instrument` `an Act` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1): the provisions of this Act apply in interpreting the instrument` `a regulation` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1): the provisions of this Act apply in interpreting the instrument` `a proclamation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 4(1A): applying the Act to regulations, rules and by-laws`

-- The three readings are by instrument. For an Act (or any other kind) the subsection says nothing.
-- src:45 | (a) a reference in this Act to the passing of an Act, or to the time of the passing of an Act, shall be construed as a reference to the making of the regulations or the time when the regulations are made, as the case may be;
@ref s 4(1A)(a) (src:45)
GIVEN `the instrument` IS A `Kind of instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 4(1A)(a): a reference in this Act to the passing of an Act, or to the time of its passing, is read, for regulations, as` `the instrument` MEANS
    IF `the instrument` EQUALS `a regulation` OR `the instrument` EQUALS `a rule` OR `the instrument` EQUALS `a by-law`
    THEN JUST "the making of the regulations or the time when the regulations are made, as the case may be"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:47 | (b) a reference in this Act to the Minister of the Crown for the time being administering an Act or enactment shall be construed as a reference to the Minister of the Crown administering the Act or enactment under which the regulations are made; and
@ref s 4(1A)(b) (src:47)
GIVEN `the instrument` IS A `Kind of instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 4(1A)(b): a reference in this Act to the Minister administering an Act or enactment is read, for regulations, as` `the instrument` MEANS
    IF `the instrument` EQUALS `a regulation` OR `the instrument` EQUALS `a rule` OR `the instrument` EQUALS `a by-law`
    THEN JUST "the Minister of the Crown administering the Act or enactment under which the regulations are made"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:49 | (c) a reference in this Act to a section or other division of an Act or to a subsection or other division of a section shall be construed as a reference to –
-- src:51 | (i) in the case of regulations, a regulation or other division of the regulations or, as the case may be, a subregulation or other division of such a regulation;
-- src:53 | (ii) in the case of rules, a rule or other division of the rules or, as the case may be, a subrule or other division of such a rule; or
-- src:55 | (iii) in the case of by-laws, a clause or other division of the by-laws or, as the case may be, a subclause or other division of such a clause.
@ref s 4(1A)(c) (src:49-55)
GIVEN `the instrument` IS A `Kind of instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 4(1A)(c): a reference in this Act to a section or other division of an Act is read as` `the instrument` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the instrument` EQUALS `a regulation` THEN JUST "a regulation or other division of the regulations"
           IF `the instrument` EQUALS `a rule` THEN JUST "a rule or other division of the rules"
           IF `the instrument` EQUALS `a by-law` THEN JUST "a clause or other division of the by-laws"
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 4(1A)(c) (src:49-55)
GIVEN `the instrument` IS A `Kind of instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 4(1A)(c): a reference in this Act to a subsection or other division of a section is read as` `the instrument` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the instrument` EQUALS `a regulation` THEN JUST "a subregulation or other division of such a regulation"
           IF `the instrument` EQUALS `a rule` THEN JUST "a subrule or other division of such a rule"
           IF `the instrument` EQUALS `a by-law` THEN JUST "a subclause or other division of such a clause"
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 4(1A)(a): a reference in this Act to the passing of an Act, or to the time of its passing, is read, for regulations, as` `a regulation` EQUALS JUST "the making of the regulations or the time when the regulations are made, as the case may be"
#ASSERT `s 4(1A)(a): a reference in this Act to the passing of an Act, or to the time of its passing, is read, for regulations, as` `an Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(1A)(b): a reference in this Act to the Minister administering an Act or enactment is read, for regulations, as` `a by-law` EQUALS JUST "the Minister of the Crown administering the Act or enactment under which the regulations are made"
#ASSERT `s 4(1A)(b): a reference in this Act to the Minister administering an Act or enactment is read, for regulations, as` `an Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(1A)(c): a reference in this Act to a section or other division of an Act is read as` `a regulation` EQUALS JUST "a regulation or other division of the regulations"
#ASSERT `s 4(1A)(c): a reference in this Act to a section or other division of an Act is read as` `a rule` EQUALS JUST "a rule or other division of the rules"
#ASSERT `s 4(1A)(c): a reference in this Act to a section or other division of an Act is read as` `a by-law` EQUALS JUST "a clause or other division of the by-laws"
#ASSERT `s 4(1A)(c): a reference in this Act to a section or other division of an Act is read as` `an order` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(1A)(c): a reference in this Act to a subsection or other division of a section is read as` `a regulation` EQUALS JUST "a subregulation or other division of such a regulation"
#ASSERT `s 4(1A)(c): a reference in this Act to a subsection or other division of a section is read as` `a rule` EQUALS JUST "a subrule or other division of such a rule"
#ASSERT `s 4(1A)(c): a reference in this Act to a subsection or other division of a section is read as` `a by-law` EQUALS JUST "a subclause or other division of such a clause"
#ASSERT `s 4(1A)(c): a reference in this Act to a subsection or other division of a section is read as` `an Act` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 4(2), (3): Acts passed after a date; the Crown`

-- src:57 | (2) Where in this Act reference is made to an Act passed after any specified date, such reference shall include every such Act, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Act.
@ref s 4(2) (src:57)
GIVEN `the day the Act was passed` IS A DATE
      `the specified date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(2): an Act is within a reference in this Act to an Act passed after a specified date` `the day the Act was passed` `the specified date` MEANS
    IF `the day the Act was passed` GREATER THAN `the specified date` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- fork: a day on or before the specified date

-- src:59 | (3) This Act shall be binding on the Crown.
@ref s 4(3) (src:59)
`s 4(3): this Act is binding on the Crown` MEANS TRUE

#ASSERT `s 4(2): an Act is within a reference in this Act to an Act passed after a specified date` (Date 2 1 1990) (Date 1 1 1990) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(2): an Act is within a reference in this Act to an Act passed after a specified date` (Date 1 1 1990) (Date 1 1 1990) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(2): an Act is within a reference in this Act to an Act passed after a specified date` (Date 31 12 1989) (Date 1 1 1990) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(3): this Act is binding on the Crown`
